1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,650
AI agents are starting to spend money.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:05,750
So who signs off?

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:10,650
This is Purser, built by Max Geurtsen.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,054
Three Claude agents run a small

5
00:00:15,104 --> 00:00:17,430
company that sells live stock data.

6
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:20,341
The Sourcing agent, on Claude Haiku, buys

7
00:00:20,391 --> 00:00:22,740
data per query, over x402 on Metal.

8
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:26,600
The Support agent, on Claude Sonnet, handles disputes and refunds.

9
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:30,820
The Treasury agent, on Claude Opus, runs FX, SWIFT and budgets.

10
00:00:30,970 --> 00:00:34,850
Each has its own Airwallex card, and its own Metal mandate.

11
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:38,356
Inside its limits, an agent pays alone.

12
00:00:38,406 --> 00:00:43,050
Beyond them, nothing moves until the CFO signs the exact terms.

13
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:49,304
Our data supplier doubles its price, from two

14
00:00:49,354 --> 00:00:51,980
to four cents a stock check, past the

15
00:00:52,030 --> 00:00:55,379
three-cent cap on the Sourcing agent's mandate.

16
00:00:55,429 --> 00:00:58,200
We let one purchase through on purpose.

17
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:01,850
Metal refused it, and the refusal is on chain.

18
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,210
Treasury proposes two ways to stay within the same twenty dollars:

19
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:08,735
raise the Sourcing agent's cap to

20
00:01:08,785 --> 00:01:10,940
four cents and keep our price,

21
00:01:11,090 --> 00:01:13,810
or raise our price to seven cents.

22
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:16,850
The CFO picks the first, with Face ID.

23
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:20,071
Eighty-six Metal payments in this run,

24
00:01:20,121 --> 00:01:23,450
each its own transaction on testnet. No emulator.

25
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:28,401
Then a customer disputes twelve orders,

26
00:01:28,451 --> 00:01:30,520
all signed by its own agent.

27
00:01:30,570 --> 00:01:33,850
Only the three with wrong data are refunded.

28
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:42,530
Anything beyond the limits goes to the CFO's phone.

29
00:01:42,580 --> 00:01:46,850
The CFO reads the exact terms, and signs with Face ID.

30
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:52,505
Six seconds later, Airwallex pays the euro

31
00:01:52,555 --> 00:01:54,905
invoice by SWIFT, in its sandbox.

32
00:01:54,955 --> 00:01:56,650
Every I.D. is published.

33
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:05,432
Now it's your turn, on the live page.

34
00:02:05,482 --> 00:02:08,978
Claude Sonnet reads the invoice, Claude Opus

35
00:02:09,028 --> 00:02:11,799
advises, and you sign with Face ID.

36
00:02:11,849 --> 00:02:13,250
Then try to cheat.

37
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:19,450
Change one cent, and the same signature is refused.

38
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:21,650
One cent. Worthless.

39
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:25,863
All twenty-four decisions by Claude.

40
00:02:25,913 --> 00:02:28,611
Sixteen stops, nothing paid over a limit:

41
00:02:28,661 --> 00:02:32,029
twelve skipped by Claude, two refused by Metal, one

42
00:02:32,079 --> 00:02:35,850
rejected by the CFO, and one planted instruction ignored.

43
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:41,421
Airwallex itself declined two charges:

44
00:02:41,471 --> 00:02:45,018
one over the limit, one in the wrong category.

45
00:02:45,068 --> 00:02:48,850
The agent asked the CFO for a raise, not a retry.

46
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:58,354
With Airwallex's Airi, agents paid with a single-use Visa credential:

47
00:02:58,404 --> 00:03:00,628
alone within the limit, above it

48
00:03:00,678 --> 00:03:02,689
only after the CFO's Face ID.

49
00:03:02,739 --> 00:03:04,963
Terms changed after that Face ID

50
00:03:05,013 --> 00:03:07,450
were refused before Airi was asked.

51
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:12,387
The agents do the work.

52
00:03:12,437 --> 00:03:15,250
The CFO signs only the exceptions.

53
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:20,312
Real: the Airwallex sandbox, Metal testnet, Claude, Face

54
00:03:20,362 --> 00:03:22,381
ID, and Airi with a test card.

55
00:03:22,431 --> 00:03:23,622
Ours or simulated:

56
00:03:23,672 --> 00:03:28,450
the suppliers, the customer, the merchant, and a test second approver.

57
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:33,050
A price shock, a dispute, a euro bill.

58
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:37,264
Claude decided, Airwallex and Metal held the limits, and

59
00:03:37,314 --> 00:03:40,350
the CFO signed only what went beyond them.

60
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:42,450
Purser. Starter Kit 11.
